.TH VNC-DISCOVERY-RESPONDER.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
vnc\-discovery\-responder.py \- mu2edaq\-discovery sidecar that advertises a VNC session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 vnc\-discovery\-responder.py
.B \-\-name
.I NAME
.B \-\-display
.I :N
.B \-\-port
.I PORT
.RB [ \-\-geometry
.IR WxH ]
.RB [ \-\-account
.IR USER ]
.RB [ \-\-announce\-interval
.IR SEC ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
VNC does not speak the mu2edaq\-discovery protocol, so
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1)
runs this sidecar beside each session.
It answers DISCOVER queries on 239.255.42.99:28999 with an ANNOUNCE
carrying
.BR app=vnc ,
.BR scheme=vnc ,
.BR version=1.0 ,
.B port
= the VNC port,
.B name
=
.RI "\(dqVNC " nodename " :N (" NAME ")\(dq"
and
.B meta
=
.RB { display ,
.BR account ,
.BR geometry },
all strings.
With a positive interval it also multicasts the ANNOUNCE unsolicited.
The advertised port listens on loopback only; a client must map it to a
configured session and tunnel to it, as
.BR crs\-gui (1)
does.
.PP
It uses
.B mu2edaq_discovery.Responder
when that package is importable by the interpreter running it \(em the
system
.BR python3 ,
not a virtual environment \(em and otherwise an embedded copy of the
protocol.
The embedded copy differs from the reference implementation: it replies
to a DISCOVER whose
.B filter
is an empty list or whose
.B qid
is absent or not a string, and a
.B filter
that is a non\-empty list or a string raises inside its receive loop,
which ends the responder thread and with it this process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
session name (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-display " :N"
display (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
VNC port (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-geometry " WxH"
included in
.B meta
when given.
.TP
.BI \-\-account " USER"
default
.BR $USER .
.TP
.BI \-\-announce\-interval " SEC"
default
.B $CRS_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL
or 30; 0 disables unsolicited announcements.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR CRS_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL ,
.BR USER .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on SIGTERM or SIGINT, and also 0 when the responder thread dies (bind
failure, or the fallback's filter crash); check the log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
python3 ~/controlroom/bin/vnc\-discovery\-responder.py \e
    \-\-name shift\-main \-\-display :2 \-\-port 5902 \-\-geometry 1920x1080
python3 \-c 'import mu2edaq_discovery'   # which implementation will run
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
